The first attempt on a centralized colonial government, based on the Articles of Confession, has many drawbacks, including the lack of a national army to enforce laws, dependable funding from required taxation, and requiring unanimity to pass any laws.

One particular event that exposed the disadvantages of the lack of strength of the colonial government is the _Shay's Rebellion_.

#lbl(<evt:shay>, event(
  "Shay's Rebellion",
)[Shay is one of the many individuals in debt as a farmer and face the possibility of losing their land to creditors. In 1787, Shays’s army, 1,200 strong, marched through the snow toward the arsenal at Springfield. The militia dispersed the mob and killed 4 of them. The scale of this event stunned the nation.])

Within the young nation, the direct cause of the rebellion, debt-ridden farmers, is present across the nation, revealing the potential of a nation-wide rebellion; outside of the nation, this event disdains the reputation of the new nation and may complicate attempts at establishing diplomatic relationships with old world nations.

On a larger scale, as mostly independent entities, states impose tax on good from other states, leading to inter-state tension.

To resolve these issues, take the perspective of microscopic actions.

